---
title: Debug menu
sidebar:
  order: 2
---

The debug menu lets you warp to any map, start any battle, and edit the player's inventory, stats, and partners while the game runs. It also has a EVT script debugger for pausing and stepping through EVT scripts.

## Turning the debug menu on or off

The debug menu is on by default. To turn it off, such as for a release, set `DX_DEBUG_MENU` to `0` in `dx/config.h`:

```c
#define DX_DEBUG_MENU 0
```

While the debug menu is on, a line at the bottom of the screen shows the map and entry the player came in through, and the player's position. In a battle, it shows the battle and the stage instead.

## Controls

While the game runs, press **D-Pad Left** to open the debug menu.

| Button | Action |
| --- | --- |
| **D-Pad Up** and **D-Pad Down** | Move between options |
| **D-Pad Left** and **D-Pad Right** | Change the selected value, or move between digits of a number |
| **R** | Select an option, or apply your changes |
| **L** | Go back to the previous menu |
| **D-Pad Right** | In the main menu, select an option |
| **D-Pad Left** or **L** | In the main menu, close the debug menu |

When you edit a number, **D-Pad Up** raises the selected digit and **D-Pad Down** lowers it.

In Diorama64, the keyboard plays the N64 controller's buttons. By default, **W**, **A**, **S**, and **D** are the D-Pad, **Q** is **L**, **E** is **R**, and **C** is **Z**. To see or change the keys, select **Game > Remap Controls...**.

## Main menu

| Option | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| **Full Restore** | Refills the player's HP, FP, and star power. |
| **Save/Load** | **Quick Save** saves the game to the current save slot, and **Quick Load** loads it. |
| **Map Select** | Warps to a map. Choose an area, then a map, then an entry number, and press **R**. |
| **Battle Select** | Starts a battle. See [Battle Select](#battle-select). |
| **Set Story Byte** | Sets the story progress, as a two-digit hexadecimal number. Press **R** to apply it. |
| **Sound Player** | Plays sound effects and music. See [Sound Player](#sound-player). |
| **Edit Partners** | Adds and removes partners and sets their levels. See [Edit Partners](#edit-partners). |
| **Edit Inventory** | Edits the player's items, equipment, and stats. See [Edit Inventory](#edit-inventory). |
| **View Collision** | Draws the map's collision. See [View Collision](#view-collision). |
| **Cheats** | Turns cheats on and off. See [Cheats](#cheats). |

If `DX_DEBUG_EVT_TESTS` is `1` in `dx/config.h`, the main menu also has **EVT Tests**, which runs DX's own tests of the EVT script interpreter.

## Battle Select

**Battle Select** has three rows. Press **D-Pad Up** or **D-Pad Down** to choose a row, and **D-Pad Left** or **D-Pad Right** to change it:

- The first row is the battle area.
- The second row is the formation in that area. The box below lists the formation's actors.
- The third row is the stage. **(auto)** uses the formation's own stage.

Press **R** to start the battle. A red row has nothing valid to choose, such as the formation row for an area with no formations, and **R** doesn't start a battle until you fix it.

## Sound Player

Select **Sound** to play sound effects by ID. Choose **Play Sound** or **Stop Sound**, enter a four-digit hexadecimal sound ID, then press **R** to play or stop that sound.

Select **Music** to browse songs by name. **D-Pad Up** and **D-Pad Down** move one song at a time, and wrap around at the ends of the list. **D-Pad Left** and **D-Pad Right** move nine songs at a time, and stop at the ends. Press **R** to play or restart the selected song, **Z** to stop the music, and **L** to go back.

## Edit Partners

Each partner has a number before its name:

| Number | Meaning |
| --- | --- |
| `-1` | Not in the party |
| `0` | In the party, at its normal rank |
| `1` | Super rank |
| `2` | Ultra rank |

Press **D-Pad Left** or **D-Pad Right** to change the selected partner's number. Press **R** to apply every partner's change. If the selected partner is in the party, it becomes the active partner.

## Edit Inventory

| Option | What it edits |
| --- | --- |
| **Items** | The player's items |
| **Badges** | The player's badges |
| **Key Items** | The player's key items |
| **Equipment** | **Boots**, **Hammer**, **Lucky Star** (whether the player has action commands), and **Star Beam** |
| **Stats** | **Max HP**, **Max FP**, **Max BP**, **Level**, and **Spirits** (the number of star power bars) |
| **Coins** | The player's coins |
| **Star Points** | The player's star points |
| **Star Pieces** | The player's star pieces |

In **Items**, **Badges**, and **Key Items**, each row is an inventory slot with a three-digit hexadecimal item ID. Select a slot and press **R** to edit its ID, then press **R** again to save the list. Press **L** to stop editing.

In **Equipment** and **Stats**, press **R** to apply your changes. Applying **Stats** also refills HP, FP, and star power.

## View Collision

Press **D-Pad Left** or **D-Pad Right** to turn an option on or off.

| Option | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| **Show Collision** | Draws the map's collision, colored by the direction each triangle faces. |
| **Cull Back** | Hides the back of one-sided collision triangles. |
| **Show Disabled** | Also draws collision that doesn't block the player. |
| **Hide Models** | Hides the map's models, so you only see the collision. |
| **Extrude Faces** | Draws each triangle pushed out slightly along the direction it faces. |
| **Highlight Floor** | Highlights the floor the player stands on. |
| **Highlight Wall** | Highlights the wall the player is touching. |
| **Near Fade Dist** | Fades out collision near the camera. `0` turns fading off, and higher numbers fade more of it. |

## Cheats

Press **D-Pad Left** or **D-Pad Right** to turn a cheat on or off.

| Cheat | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| **God Mode** | In battle, the player's and partner's attacks deal 99 damage, and enemies' attacks deal none. |
| **Speed Mode** | The player walks and runs three times as fast, and enemies in the world can't touch the player. |
| **Fly With L** | Hold **L** to rise into the air. |
| **High Jump** | The player jumps higher. |
| **Ignore Walls** | The player walks through walls. |

## EVT script debugger

The EVT script debugger pauses EVT scripts and runs them one command at a time. To open it, press **D-Pad Right** while the debug menu is closed. To close it, press **D-Pad Right** or **L**.

The list on the left shows every EVT script that's running. **Grp** is the EVT script's group, **Start** is the address of its first command, and **Current** is how far the current command is from the start. A paused EVT script is red.

The menu on the right has these options:

| Option | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| **Attach** | Choose an EVT script from the list to inspect and step through. |
| **Break** | Choose an EVT script from the list to pause. |
| **Resume** | Choose a paused EVT script from the list to carry on. |
| **Break All** | Pauses every EVT script. |
| **Resume All** | Carries on every EVT script. |

For **Attach**, **Break**, and **Resume**, press **D-Pad Up** or **D-Pad Down** to choose an EVT script from the list, then press **R**.

### Stepping through an EVT script

When you attach to an EVT script, the menu changes:

| Option | What it does |
| --- | --- |
| **Detach** | Stops inspecting the EVT script, and goes back to the list. |
| **Break** or **Resume** | Pauses the EVT script, or carries it on. |
| **Step Once** | Runs the current command for one frame, then pauses. |
| **Step Over** | Runs the current command until it finishes, then pauses. Use it for a command that takes more than one frame, such as `Wait`. |
| **Vars** | Changes how the box shows variables: **Int**, **Fixed**, **Float**, or **Raw** (hexadecimal). |

The box on the left shows **Vars** or **Disasm**. Press **D-Pad Left** or **D-Pad Right** to switch between them:

- **Vars** shows the EVT script's local variables, `LVar0` to `LVarF`, and its four function temporaries. A value that changed since the last step is green.
- **Disasm** shows the EVT script's commands, numbered, with the current command in green.

To pause an EVT script at a particular command, put a `BreakPoint` command in it. When the EVT script reaches it, the EVT script pauses, and you can attach to it in the EVT script debugger.

## Performance profiler

To turn on the performance profiler, set `USE_PROFILER` to `1` in `dx/config.h`:

```c
#define USE_PROFILER 1
```

In the game, press **L** and **D-Pad Up** together to show or hide it.
